      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your pain is real and valid, but a life of being \"okay\" is not equivalent to failing to reach a peak you never set out to climb; it is simply a deeply exhausted journey of finding strength in small, consistent steps. Many of the most resilient people in history found that their dignity didn't come from changing the world, but from refusing to let others' expectations define their right to exist. Give yourself permission to stop measuring your story against a ghost's greatest hits and instead start writing your own chapter in the quiet, steady rhythm of your own presence.",
